.Dd September 19, 2026
.Dt UNAME 2
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm uname ,
.Nm sethostname ,
.Nm sysinfo
.Nd get system identity and statistics or set the host name
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/utsname.h
.Ft int
.Fn uname "struct utsname *buf"
.In unistd.h
.Ft int
.Fn sethostname "const char *name" "size_t len"
.In sys/sysinfo.h
.Ft int
.Fn sysinfo "struct sysinfo *info"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn uname
writes the system identity to
.Fa buf .
The six fields are 65-byte arrays containing null-terminated strings:
.Bl -tag -width "domainname"
.It Va sysname
.Ql Rach2 .
.It Va nodename
The mutable host name, initially
.Ql rach2 .
.It Va release
.Ql 1.0.0 .
.It Va version
.Ql "Rach2 musl port" .
.It Va machine
.Ql i686 .
.It Va domainname
.Ql (none) .
Musl exposes this field as
.Va domainname
with
.Dv _GNU_SOURCE
defined, and as
.Va __domainname
otherwise.
.El
.Pp
.Fn sethostname
copies
.Fa len
bytes from
.Fa name
and appends a null byte to set the single system host name.
The length must be from 0 through 64.
A length of 0 sets an empty name without reading
.Fa name .
The name is returned in
.Fn uname Ns 's
.Va nodename
field and by musl's
.Fn gethostname .
The handler makes no uid check.
.Pp
.Fn sysinfo
writes the 64-byte i386 system statistics structure to
.Fa info .
It reports:
.Bl -tag -width "totalram, freeram"
.It Va uptime
Seconds since boot.
.It Va procs
The number of process records, including unreaped children.
.It Va totalram , freeram
Total managed and free physical RAM, from the frame counts, in bytes.
.It Va mem_unit
1.
.It Va loads
Three zeros; load averages are not tracked.
.It Va sharedram , bufferram , totalswap , freeswap , totalhigh , freehigh
Zero.
.El
.Pp
The i386 system call numbers are 122 for
.Fn uname ,
74 for
.Fn sethostname ,
and 116 for
.Fn sysinfo .
The pointer is passed in EBX; for
.Fn sethostname ,
ECX contains the length.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
These functions return 0 on success, or -1 on failure with
.Va errno
set.
The kernel returns a negative error number on failure.
.Sh EXAMPLES
The default suite's
.Pa tests/miscprobe.c
calls
.Fn sysinfo
and checks that
.Va procs
is at least 1 and
.Va mem_unit
is 1.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width "[EINVAL]"
.It Bq Er EFAULT
The result of
.Fn uname
or
.Fn sysinfo
cannot be written to user memory, or
.Fn sethostname
cannot read the specified name bytes.
.It Bq Er EINVAL
The length passed to
.Fn sethostname
is outside the range 0 through 64.
.El
